  "id": "COMPOUND:30081 - PROTEIN:5792",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Ergosta-7,22-Dien-3-One may be involved in the biological pathway leading to RWLeu4 through multiple indirect mechanisms. The first path links Ergosta-7,22-Dien-3-One to Replicase polyprotein 1ab, which is targeted by Surangin D, and ultimately to RWLeu4. The second path connects Ergosta-7,22-Dien-3-One to Carboxylesterase 2, which is targeted by a complex compound and also leads to RWLeu4. The third path shows that Ergosta-7,22-Dien-3-One targets VMRC-LCP, which is targeted by 7-Angeloylechinatine, also leading to RWLeu4. These findings collectively suggest that Ergosta-7,22-Dien-3-One may act as a mediator in a pathway that ultimately influences RWLeu4 through different molecular interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Ergosta-7,22-Dien-3-One to play a role in a broader biological process that involves multiple targets, possibly through enzyme activity or receptor interaction. The evidence supports a plausible mechanism where Ergosta-7,22-Dien-3-One may serve as a central node in a network of interactions that ultimately affect RWLeu4.",
